Mark entry and post-lock in startMatching

run-293's panel ends on a probeCandidates return: the matching call goes back to
its caller and nothing follows.  startMatching locks arbitration first, so one
line either side of that lock says whether the stall is the lock or the loop.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
index 6d7dd7e..4be2404 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -1076,7 +1076,9 @@ IOService::startMatching( IOOptionBits options )
 	bool        sync;
 	bool        waitAgain;
 
+	printf("\nnio: SM enter t=%p", current_thread());
 	lockForArbitration();
+	printf("\nnio: SM locked t=%p", current_thread());
 
 	sync = (options & kIOServiceSynchronous)
 	    || ((provider = getProvider())
